enus: read in-word enye with the palatal nasal

US English letter rules never learned to spell the enye:
normalize_eng_letters folds it to a plain n, so pinata comes out
pinata. Standing alone it is the letters name already, through
dictionary eng_char_name, and is left alone. In-word units, Western
0xF1/0xD1 or UTF-8, become ny/Ny, which n_rules and y_rules read
as the authentic nj sound, exactly like the hardcoded senor entries
already do. Other languages keep their bytes: Spanish reads the
letter natively.
Applied at build time so CI builds the same tree.
